licy requires cyclophosphamide trial before belimumab, rule_6a24180be8 creates an exception when the next required step poses greater clinical risk than disease progression. The documented progression to nephrotic-range proteinuria and the dual recommendation to bypass cyclophosphamide due to risk/benefit calculus satisfy this exception. Conclusion: Standard step-therapy denial would be appropriate under policy; however, rule_6a24180be8 applies and overrides that denial based on documented specialist consensus that proceeding directly to belimumab reduces overall clinical risk compared to mandating cyclophosphamide in a patient with worsening renal function.",
